  [', '--- Source 2 ---\nFile: eval/evaluate_ragas.py\nType: source_code\nPriority: 5\nContent:\n1: """"""\n2: Evaluates retrieval and generation quality SEPARATELY using the RAGAS\n3: framework, closing a gap the other two eval scripts don\'t cover:\n4: evaluate_correctness.py only scores the final answer, so a low score there\n5: doesn\'t tell you whether retrieval fetched the wrong chunks or generation\n6: misused the right ones. This script scores each stage on its own:\n7: \n8:     - Context Precision : are the retrieved chunks actually relevant to the\n9:                            question, with the relevant ones ranked higher?\n10:                            (retrieval quality)\n11:     - Faithfulness      : does the generated answer only state things\n12:                            actually supported by the retrieved chunks, or\n13:                            does it hallucinate beyond them?\n14:                            (generation quality)\n15:     - Response Relevancy: does the generated answer actually address the\n16:                            question asked, rather than going off-topic?\n17:                            (generation quality)\n18: \n19: All three metrics are reference-free (no hand-written ground truth needed),\n20: so this reuses the same golden questions as evaluate_correctness.py — only\n21: the questions, not the key_facts, since those aren\'t needed here.\n22: \n23: IMPORTANT — like the other eval scripts, this is completely standalone:\n24:     - Never imported by app.py, has ZERO effect on live app behavior.\n25:     - Clones its own throwaway copy of the target repo and deletes its\n26:       vector store when done.\n27: \n28: Usage:\n29:     python -m eval.evaluate_ragas\n30: \n31: Requires GROQ_API_KEY in your environment/.env (used both for running the\n32: real pipeline AND as the judge LLM for RAGAS\'s metrics — no OpenAI key', '--- Source 3 ---\nFile: eval/golden_correctness_questions.py\nType: source_code\nPriority: 5\nContent:\n85:             ""Hybrid search is listed as a future enhancement, not something already implemented"",\n86:         ],\n87:     ),\n88:     (\n89:         ""How does the system decide which retrieval strategy to use for a question?"",\n90:         [\n91:             ""An LLM-powered query router classifies the question into a category"",\n92:             ""The category determines which retrievers/document types are used"",\n93:         ],\n94:     ),\n95: ]', '--- Source 4 ---\nFile: README.md\nType: readme\nPriority: 1\nContent:\n192: \n193: **Step 13 — Merge & Deduplicate**\n194: The retrieved documents are merged and deduplicated.\n195: \n196: **Step 14 — Reranking**\n197: Each surviving chunk is scored by a **cross-encoder reranker** against the (rewritten) question, producing a `reranker_score`. This re-orders results by actual relevance rather than raw vector-similarity alone, correcting cases where embedding search alone would surface a superficially similar but less useful chunk.\n198: \n199: **Step 15 — Priority-Aware Sorting**\n200: The reranked documents are sorted using a combination of reranker score and file priority before being passed to the LLM.\n201: \n202: **Step 16 — Answer Generation**\n203: The Groq LLM (Llama 3.3 70B Versatile) generates a response using only the retrieved, reranked repository context, and returns a source-aware answer.\n204: \n205: ---\n206: \n207: ## ✨ Example Questions\n208: \n209: **Overview**\n210: - What is Flask?\n211: - What problem does this project solve?\n212: - Explain this project.\n213: \n214: **Architecture**\n215: - Explain the project architecture.\n216: - Explain the folder structure.\n217: - What are the main modules?\n218: \n219: **Implementation**', '--- Source 5 ---\nFile: eval/evaluate_ragas.py\nType: source_code\nPriority: 5\nContent:\n180:         groq_api_key=groq_api_key,\n181:         model_name=""llama-3.1-8b-instant"",\n182:         temperature=0\n183:     ))\n184:     judge_embeddings = LangchainEmbeddingsWrapper(get_embedding_model())\n185: \n186:     dataset = EvaluationDataset(samples=samples)\n187: \n188:     print(""\\nScoring with RAGAS (Context Precision, Faithfulness, Response Relevancy)...\\n"")\n189: \n190:     # RAGAS defaults to 16 concurrent judge calls (max_workers), which\n191:     # overwhelms Groq\'s rate limits. Faithfulness needs multiple sequential\n192:     # LLM calls per sample (claim decomposition, then verification), so it\n193:     # kept timing out even at max_workers=3 -- Groq\'s per-minute rate limit\n194:     # forces retries that eat into the timeout budget once several of\n195:     # Faithfulness\'s extra calls are in flight at once. Fully serial\n196:     # (max_workers=1) removes that contention entirely: slower overall, but\n197:     # every job gets a real score instead of some silently landing as NaN.\n198:     run_config = RunConfig(max_workers=1, timeout=180)\n199: \n200:     result = evaluate(\n201:         dataset=dataset,\n202:         metrics=[\n203:             LLMContextPrecisionWithoutReference(),\n204:             Faithfulness(),\n205:             ResponseRelevancy(),\n206:         ],\n207:         llm=judge_llm,\n208:         embeddings=judge_embeddings,\n209:         run_config=run_config,\n210:     )\n211: \n212:     scores_df = result.to_pandas()\n213:     scores_df.insert(1, ""category"", categories)\n214: \n215:     # --- Write results to CSV ---\n216:     csv_path = os.path.join(os.path.dirname(__file__), ""ragas_eval_results.csv"")\n217:     scores_df.to_csv(csv_path, index=False)\n218: \n219:     # --- Summary ---\n220:     precision_col = ""llm_context_precision_without_reference""', '--- Source 6 ---\nFile: README.md\nType: readme\nPriority: 1\nContent:\n23: \n24: ---\n25: \n26: ## 🏗️ System Architecture\n27: \n28: ```\n29:             GitHub Repository URL\n30:                       │\n31:                       ▼\n32:              Clone Repository\n33:                       │\n34:                       ▼\n35:             Load Repository Files\n36:                       │\n37:                       ▼\n38:         Generate Repository Structure\n39:                       │\n40:                       ▼\n41:       Code & Documentation Chunking\n42:                       │\n43:                       ▼\n44:           Generate Vector Embeddings\n45:                       │\n46:                       ▼\n47:              Store in ChromaDB\n48:                       │\n49:                       ▼\n50:              User Asks Question\n51:                       │\n52:                       ▼\n53:          Question Rewriting (LLM)\n54:                       │\n55:                       ▼\n56:            Query Router (LLM)\n57:                       │\n58:                       ▼\n59:           Multi-Retriever Search\n60:                       │\n61:      ┌──────────┬──────────┬──────────┐\n62:      │          │          │          │\n63:      ▼          ▼          ▼          ▼']",The final answer is generated by **Groq’s Llama 3.3 70B Versatile model**【Source 1†L50-L53】【Source 4†L202-L204】.,0.7499999999625,1.0,0.7305214818291383
